0..76 Comment "//! Rose trees: a node holds its children, in two forms. Written directly, a"
77..156 Comment "//! node holds a `List` of nodes: the list\'s parameter is strictly positive, so"
157..237 Comment "//! each child stands below the node and the family declares; a measure recurses"
238..318 Comment "//! through the list\'s `map`, which a call instantiates at the children\'s stage,"
319..398 Comment "//! and a run passes `map` the children\'s type as a code. Written as a block, a"
399..479 Comment "//! node holds a forest and a forest is empty or a tree before a forest: the two"
480..560 Comment "//! families name each other, so they are one block, admitted as one and sharing"
561..638 Comment "//! one stage; and the two measures name each other, so they are one fixpoint"
639..711 Comment "//! over the sum of their domains, each measure that fixpoint at its own"
712..788 Comment "//! summand. A measure may take a parameter after the tree, and the fixpoint"
789..863 Comment "//! passes it on. A call through either stands one stage below the node or"
864..941 Comment "//! forest it was read from [Abel-2004-termination_checking_with_types]. What"
942..1013 Comment "//! the direct form refuses is in `../../pathological/data/rose.gandr`."
1014..1017 Comment "//!"
1018..1098 Comment "//! - see: #3722 — a measure passes a parameter after the tree to its sibling,"
1099..1151 Comment "//!   by which `treeWeight` and `forestWeight` check"
1152..1178 Comment "//! - see: #517 — `Bush`"
1179..1206 Comment "//! - see: #393 — `nodes`"
1207..1255 Comment "//! - see: #452 — `shrub_nodes`, `grown_nodes`"
1256..1312 Comment "//! - cites: [Abel-2004-termination_checking_with_types]"
1313..1316 Comment "//!"
1317..1441 Comment "//! [Abel-2004-termination_checking_with_types]: https://doi.org/10.1051/ita:2004015 \"Abel, Termination checking with types\""
1443..1515 Comment "// The naturals the measures count in, their addition, and the lists the"
1516..1545 Comment "// direct form nests through."
